2026-11-06T03:02:45.0126284Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0134924Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0135781Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0136325Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0136594Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0136921Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0137220Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0137480Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0138120Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0138479Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0138679Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0139057Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0139348Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0139711Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0140274Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:02:45.0140509Z 
